lenging especially  when they don't have a lot of experience  their emotions can get the best of them  and they can have a hard time  remembering their lines but that wasn't  the case for twin actors dylan and Cole  Sprouse who posed as Ross's son Ben on  friends and this behind-the-scenes  moment we see one of the Sprouse twins  helping Jennifer Anniston out with her  lines in the episode the one with the  truth about London I was I was your  daddy's girlfriend but you're not  anymore  after schooling Jennifer in front of the  entire crew Jennifer breaks the fourth  wall by giving the camera a wide-eyed  look but this wouldn't be the last time  that a Strauss twin reminded one of his  co-stars of their lines  David's on-screen son reminds him of his  lines in the episode the one with the  holiday armadillo but he doesn't stop  there the kid actor jokingly says man I  know all of his lines it looks like  dylan and Cole Sprouse were professional  actors from the get-go  the one where Cortney pulls a Monica  Courtney Cox did an amazing job at  portraying her eccentric character  Monica Geller  what if there's no room for a ribbon  drawer because the baby stuff takes up  all of the space but after years of  stepping into her shoes Courtney adopted  Monica's special personality in the  episode the one with the cooking class  Monica's restaurant receives a bad  review prompting her to take a cooking  class with Joey this hilarious episode  had us laughing the whole way through  and so did it's gay grill Courtney  pulled a Monica when she was asked to  reshoot a scene from the beginning the  actors captain messing up her lines  instead of doing what the director asked  she started arguing with him both matt  LeBlanc and Matthew Perry laughed at  Courtney as she begged producers to let  it slide and Matt mocks Courtney behind  her back  Matthew tried to argue with Monica  during her prima donna moment but she  clapped back saying that he had just  messed up his lines a bunch of times  just moments before this  behind-the-scenes moment could have been  a scene from friends itself turns out  that Courtney Matt and Matthew are a lot  like the characters they portray on the  show the one where it tastes like feet  during an interview with Conan O'Brien  the cast of friends were asked to reveal  some of their funnies behind the scenes  moment and well there were just so many  to choose from  Conan revealed that after long hours of  filming the cast would often laugh at  how one of their fellow actors  pronounced a certain word and since no  one pronounces words like Ross this  often happens when it was David's turn  to speak in season 6 episode 9 Monica  tasks Rachel with making a trifle and  she messes up the recipe when Ross takes  a bite of the trifle / shepherd's pie he  announces Victor's retreat well as Conan  pointed out the way David said the word  feed send the friends cast into  hysterics Matt could not stop laughing  at this word which made filming the  trifle seen all the more challenging  this blooper is even funnier than the  real scene we can't decide what's  funnier the actual front show or what  went on behind the scenes before you go  tell us who your favorite cast member is  in the comment section below give this  video a big thumbs up if you love  friends thanks for watching the things  we'll see you soon  [Music]
 

